note as narchived #FFF0F0
  <b>What used to be here.</b>

  This diagram was "the live path": two phones
  paired over BLE / Wi-Fi P2P, sharing a timebase
  via ClockSync, triangulating through StereoEngine
  and calling the ball mid-rally without the server.

  Archived 2026-07-27 — Sources/Peer/, Sources/Stereo/
  and the Live/ pairing stack now live under
  archive/stereo/ios/. Restore point: tag
  archive/stereo-v1.

  Why: triangulation needs the ball found in <i>both</i>
  views, and single-view wall-hit recall is ~35%, so
  stereo multiplied the bottleneck instead of fixing it.
  Revisit gate: single-view wall-hit recall ~85%.
end note

note as ndiff #FFFDF0
  <b>Native (here)  ..versus..  web (diagrams 3 & 4)</b>

  capture   : in-app 4K60, locked   / file upload
  detection : on-device, overlay only / server RF-DETR, authoritative
  judging   : server, after upload  / server, after upload
  result    : a run dir you review  / a run dir you review

  Both surfaces end in the same place. The native app
  buys capture control, not a different pipeline.
end note

@enduml


' ===========================================================================
'  7 of 7 — DATA SHAPES
'  These are plain dicts and CSV rows. Nothing declares them. This is the
'  map you would otherwise build by print()ing things.
' ===========================================================================
@startuml data_shapes
title The records that flow between stages\n<size:11>//Mostly plain dicts and CSV rows — nothing in the code declares these//</size>

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #666666
}

class "CSV detection row" as row <<ball_coordinates.csv>> #EEF4FF {
  <size:10>tracking_common.CSV_FIELDNAMES</size>
  ..
  source_frame : int
  timestamp_seconds : float
  detected : bool
  class_name : str
  confidence : float
  x_center, y_center : float
  width, height : float
  x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max : float
  --
  <size:10>One row per frame examined.</size>
  <size:10>The interchange format between the</size>
  <size:10>tracking pass and every detector.</size>
}

class "Detected hit" as hit <<dict>> #FFF6EC {
  hit_frame : int
  timestamp_seconds : float
  score : float
  candidate_x, candidate_y : float
  detector : str
  event_type : "wall"|"racket"|"floor"|"side_wall"
  ..votes / fusion also carry..
  impact_x, impact_y : float
  impact_frame, impact_time
  method, diagnostics
  audio_assisted : bool
}

class "Judged hit (the verdict)" as verdict <<dict>> #EEF9F0 {
  frame : int
  timestamp_seconds : float
  **call : "IN" | "OUT" | None**
  **reason : str**
  judge_source : "impact_estimate"|"detected_center"
  margin_px : float
  ..
  wall_diagram : {x, y, ...}
  target_zone : 1..8
  court_position_ft, floor_zone
  velocity : {speed_before, speed_after, ...}
  rally_number, player_number
  --
  <size:10>call is None for racket/floor/side_wall.</size>
  <size:10><b>Verdicts are front-wall-only.</b></size>
}

class Point <<frozen dataclass>> #F6EEFF {
  x : float
  y : float
}

class Line <<frozen dataclass>> #F6EEFF {
  left : Point
  right : Point
  --
  y_at_x(x)
  point_at(u)
  **signed_distance_below(point)**
  <size:10>perpendicular signed distance —</size>
  <size:10>which is why a tilted calibration</size>
  <size:10>still judges correctly</size>
}

class WallCorners <<frozen dataclass>> #F6EEFF {
  top_left, top_right : Point
  bottom_right, bottom_left : Point
  --
  x_bounds_at_y(y)
  <size:10>Top corners = OUT line × side walls (15 ft).</size>
  <size:10>Bottom = wall/floor seam. All four have exact</size>
  <size:10>court coordinates, so they double as</size>
  <size:10>camera-pose correspondences.</size>
}

class CameraModel #F6EEFF {
  focal_px : float
  center_px : (float, float)
  rotation : 3x3  <size:10>world→camera</size>
  camera_center_ft : (3,)
  distortion : dict | None
  fit_rms_px : float | None
  frame_width, frame_height
}

class FloorMap #F6EEFF {
  homography_court_from_image : 3x3
  fit_rms_px, max_residual_px
  landmark_count : int
  --
  image_to_court(px) → feet
}

class "job.json" as job <<the run record>> #F4F4F4 {
  run_id, run_dir
  **status : queued|running|complete|failed**
  **stage : coarse|refine|judging|complete**
  message : str
  video_path, start_frame, end_frame, fps
  frame_stride, inference_width
  event_engine, fusion_3d
  processed_frames, total_frames
  hits : [Judged hit]
  target_zones, floor_zones
  hits_error, error
  ..provenance, always recorded..
  model_id, tracking_backend, device
  app_version
}

class "calibration.json" as cal <<squash-calibration-v2>> #F4F4F4 {
  lines : {out, tin}
  wall_corners : 4 points
  floor : landmarks + homography
  frame_width, frame_height
  <size:10>exactly as the browser posted it</size>
}

class "corrections.json" as corr <<corrections-v2>> #F4F4F4 {
  frame : int
  corrected : {type, call, ball{x,y},
       frame_is_bounce, frame} | null
  predicted : {type, call, source,
       margin_px, ball}
  agrees : {type, call, frame}
  recorded_at, app_version
  <size:10>one entry per frame, latest wins.</size>
  <size:10>corrected = null means "undo".</size>
}

row --> hit : bounce engine\n<size:10>gb_model | votes | fusion</size>
hit --> verdict : judge_hits()
Line --> verdict : judge_ball(point, out, tin, corners)
WallCorners --> verdict
Point --* Line
Point --* WallCorners
cal --> Line : parsed into
cal --> WallCorners
cal --> CameraModel : solve_camera_model()
cal --> FloorMap : load_floor_calibration()
CameraModel ..> hit : fusion_3d only\n<size:10>(ballistic arcs in court feet)</size>
FloorMap --> verdict : floor events →\ncourt_position_ft
verdict --* job
verdict ..> corr : the human disagrees

note as nprov #FFFDF0
  <b>Why job.json records model_id / backend / device / app_version:</b>
  so any result can be attributed to the model version that
  produced it. When a number looks wrong, check the provenance
  before you check the algorithm.
end note
nprov .. job

@enduml
